        "cardIndex": 2,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Cyber Insurance & Digital Identity Protection (Part 2)",
        "content": "| Insurance Company | Policy Marketing Name | Sum Insured Range Options | Annual Premium Range | Key Highlight Features |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Bajaj Allianz** | Cyber Safe Insurance | ₹1 Lakh to ₹1 Crore | **₹1,200 to ₹3,500 / year** | Covers 11 major cyber risks, identity theft, malware restoration, counseling cost |\n| **HDFC ERGO** | Cyber Sahi Hai Policy | ₹50,000 to ₹5 Lakhs | **₹800 to ₹2,200 / year** | Zero deductible on financial fraud, fast app-based claim settlement within 7 days |\n| **ICICI Lombard** | Individual Cyber Insurance | ₹1 Lakh to ₹25 Lakhs | **₹1,000 to ₹3,000 / year** | Social media hacking restoration, legal defense cost, 24x7 cyber helpline |\n| **SBI General** | Cyber Vault Insurance | ₹1 Lakh to ₹10 Lakhs | **₹900 to ₹2,500 / year** | Loss of wages during cyber investigation covered, e-reputation restoration cover |\n\n#### Cyber Insurance Claim Filing Step-by-Step SLA Roadmap:\n\n```\n[Incident Occurs] ──> [Call 1930 & File Cyber Complaint within 2 hours] ──> [Obtain Police FIR] ──> [Notify Insurer within 7 Days] ──> [Submit IT Forensics / Statements] ──> [Claim Reimbursement]\n```\n\n#### Student Cost-Benefit Analysis:\n₹1,000 Per Year Premium ka matlab hai **Keval ₹2.70 Per Day!** Canteen ki ek cold drink ya coffee ki keemat mein aap poore saal ke liye ₹1 Lakh se ₹3 Lakh tak ke digital cyber frauds se completely risk-free ho sakte ho!\n\n---\n\n### 23.3.3 Identity Theft Recovery Protocol\n\nAao ek nightmarish scenario imagine karte hain:\n**Sneha** ko ek din CIBIL score alert app par notification aata hai ki uski CIBIL credit rating **780 se drop hokar 590** ho gayi hai. Jab woh detailed report check karti hai, toh pata chalta hai ki kisi unknown Instant Fake Loan App ne Sneha ke leaked PAN Card par **₹60,000 ka personal loan** le rakha hai jo 3 mahine se non-payment default status dikha raha hai!\n\nAgar aapke saath aisa identity theft fraud ho jaaye, toh panic karne ki jagah **The 7-Step Emergency Identity Recovery Protocol** follow karo:\n\n```\n[1. Call 1930 / Cyber Portal] ──> [2. File Police Zero FIR] ──> [3. Serve Fraud Notice to Lender]\n                                                                        │\n[6. CIBIL Score Dispute] <── [5. Escalate RBI Ombudsman] <── [4. Freeze & Re-issue Credentials]\n```\n\n#### The 7-Step Operational Action Roadmap:\n\n1. **Step 1: Emergency Reporting within Golden Hour:**\n   - Immediately call **National Cyber Crime Helpline Number: 1930** (Government of India Helpline).\n   - Log complaint on official portal: `cybercrime.gov.in`. Get an official **Acknowledgement Number**.\n2. **Step 2: File Zero FIR at Cyber Police Station:**\n   - Nearest Cyber Crime Cell ya local Police Station jaakar written complaint do aur **FIR (First Information Report)** copy receive karo with official stamp & signature.\n3. **Step 3: Serve Legal Fraud Notice to Fraudulent Lender / NBFC:**\n   - Loan Dene wali company / Bank ke Principal Nodal Grievance Officer ko Email aur Registered AD Speed Post se legal notice bhejo.\n   - Attachments: Cyber Crime Acknowledgement Copy + Police FIR Copy + Self Declaration Affidavit stating: *\"I have never applied for or received proceeds of Loan Account No. XYZ. This is a case of criminal identity theft.\"*\n4. **Step 4: Lock/Freeze Affected Identity Credentials:**\n   - UIDAI portal se Aadhaar Biometrics instantly lock karo. e-PAN duplicate reissue application submit karo.\n5. **Step 5: Escalate to RBI Integrated Ombudsman (The Master Weapon):**\n   - Agar Bank / NBFC 30 din ke andar aapke naam se fraudulent loan cancel nahi karti aur recovery agents se harassment karwati hai, toh direct RBI Portal: `cms.rbi.org.in` par complaint file kardo.\n   - *RBI Circular Protection:* Under RBI Circular on Customer Liability in Unauthorized Electronic Banking Transactions (DBR.No.Leg.BC.78/09.07.005/2017-18), identity theft aur prompt reporting ke case mein **Victim ki ZERO LIABILITY hoti hai!** Bank/NBFC ko loan account closed mark karna padega!\n6. **Step 6: Credit Bureau CIBIL Dispute Filing:**\n   - CIBIL, Experian, aur Equifax portals par dispute raise karke credit report se fake loan entry permanently remove karwao.\n7. **Step 7: Cyber Insurance Claim Reimbursement:**\n   - Cyber Insurance company ko incident report karke legal expenses aur financial losses reimbursement request log karo.\n\n#### Draft Template: Fraudulent Loan Identity Theft Notice to Bank/NBFC\n\n```text\nTo,\nThe Principal Nodal Officer / Grievance Redressal Cell,\n[Bank / NBFC Name Limited],\n[City, State]\n\nSubject: NOTICE OF CRIMINAL IDENTITY THEFT & FRAUDULENT LOAN DISBURSAL (Loan Account No: __________)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI, [Your Full Name], residing at [Your Address], holding PAN: [Your PAN Number] and Aadhaar: [Last 4 digits], hereby bring to your immediate notice that a fraudulent loan account bearing Account No. [Loan Account Number] amounting to Rs. [Amount] has been illegally opened using my stolen identity credentials without my knowledge, consent, or authorization.",
